(7675358, 1254351, 77543, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> Handy location to have on your doorstep. Is that the official line? Congrats on the HM! </i></td></tr></table> Yes, it''s just outside the old Greenwich Observatory. A good place to check the accuracy of the GPS data. This is what my camera recorded at the time of the shot<br/> <br/>Latitude 51,28.6196N<br/>Longitude 0,0.0788W<br/> <br/>If you put the coordinates into Google Map you''ll see how far out the camera''s location was. The picture was a shot of "The Avenue" just south of the Observatory.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-09-25 05:55:14.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Handy location to have on your doorstep. Is that the official line? Congrats on the HM!  Yes, it''s just outside the old Greenwich Observatory. A good place to check the accuracy of the GPS data. This is what my camera recorded at the time of the shot Latitude 51,28.6196NLongitude 0,0.0788W If you put the coordinates into Google Map you''ll see how far out the camera''s location was. The picture was a shot of "The Avenue" just south of the Observatory.', '2020-09-25 06:49:57.000000', '2020-09-25 06:55:14.000000', 0),
(7675359, 1254351, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DistantColours:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> Handy location to have on your doorstep. Is that the official line? Congrats on the HM! </i></td></tr></table> Yes, it''s just outside the old Greenwich Observatory. A good place to check the accuracy of the GPS data. This is what my camera recorded at the time of the shot<br/> <br/>Latitude 51,28.6196N<br/>Longitude 0,0.0788W<br/> <br/>If you put the coordinates into Google Map you''ll see how far out the camera''s location was. The picture was a shot of "The Avenue" just south of the Observatory. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you - I had never thought of comparing my camera GPS data with the google map location.</td>', 'Originally posted by DistantColours: Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Handy location to have on your doorstep. Is that the official line? Congrats on the HM!  Yes, it''s just outside the old Greenwich Observatory. A good place to check the accuracy of the GPS data. This is what my camera recorded at the time of the shot Latitude 51,28.6196NLongitude 0,0.0788W If you put the coordinates into Google Map you''ll see how far out the camera''s location was. The picture was a shot of "The Avenue" just south of the Observatory.   Thank you - I had never thought of comparing my camera GPS data with the google map location.', '2020-09-25 07:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
